<ShowcaseLayout title="About" description="The purpose, principles and provenance of the Arifian Design System.">
  <section class="page-intro page-width"><p class="eyebrow">ARIFIAN DESIGN SYSTEM</p><h1>About the system.</h1><p>A personal visual language for useful interfaces. Built by Arifian Saputra, with the same warm surfaces, sharp edges and editorial rhythm as the portfolio.</p></section>
  <div class="prose-grid page-width">
    <aside><p class="eyebrow">TERRACOTTA<br />MINIMALIST BRUTALISM</p><p>Room to read.<br />Clear ways forward.</p><a class="text-link" href="/foundations/">Explore the foundations ↗</a></aside>
    <div class="prose-stack"><section><h2>A system you can explore.</h2><p>The smallest decisions shape the whole interface: the weight of a heading, the edge of a field, the space before an action. This showcase brings those decisions together in working components and compositions.</p><p>The portfolio provides the visual starting point. The collection extends that language to forms, navigation, records, feedback and application patterns.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Consistency with room to adapt.</h2><p>Lexend Deca headings and Inclusive Sans body text sit on parchment and ivory. Terracotta marks moments of attention. Borders define structure; asymmetry gives larger compositions their rhythm.</p><p>Light and dark appearances share the same geometry. Keyboard focus, readable labels and a complete static motion mode are part of the design.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Clear provenance.</h2><p>Locally customized shadcn and Base UI primitives provide the control foundation. Motion powers bounded transitions. Original compositions interpret the portfolio’s visual language using independently authored sample content.</p><p>Each specimen identifies its origin and license context. “Arifian Original” describes authorship; it does not grant a third-party license. All catalog entries remain previews pending the full browser and visual review.</p></section>
    <section><h2>A place to try things.</h2><p>Projects, people, metrics and conversations here are synthetic. Form submissions and messages stay in memory. The examples let you inspect behavior without connecting to a service.</p><div class="cluster"><a class="text-link" href="/originals/">Meet the originals ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="/patterns/">Explore patterns ↗</a></div></section></div>
  </div>
</ShowcaseLayout>
